  {
   "k": "1gmb1ef",
   "en": "\"Force a Japanese surrender\" means \"kick Japan off the continent and ⟦0⟧ a white peace with them\". Rejecting the white peace and trying to capitulate them instead will not trigger the achievement.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "29c0fd",
   "en": "accept"
  },
  {
   "k": "ufly9f",
   "en": "Method 1"
  },
  {
   "k": "ryqotm",
   "en": "Do not accept cooperation with ⟦0⟧ until the ⟦1⟧ are about to attack. Then, form the Chinese United Front and accept all invites. Quickly rush to Korea and push them off the continent. After they have offered peace, accept it, and kick Communist China from your faction. Declare on them and annex them as soon as possible, before they start war against you. Do the same with the other faction members, leaving ⟦2⟧ for last.",
   "frags": 3
  },
  {
   "k": "8eaarh",
   "en": "Communist China"
  },
  {
   "k": "152t0ju",
   "en": "Japanese"
  },
  {
   "k": "1apefkn",
   "en": "Sinkiang"
  },
  {
   "k": "upljye",
   "en": "Method 2"
  },
  {
   "k": "1jh0m08",
   "en": "As above, fight as United Chinese Front (or alone, if the Front does not form for some reason) until Japan white-peaces. Do \"One China Policy\", which disbands the faction. Declare on all warlords one by one. If Japan is still around, they'll join its faction, but Japan won't go to war with you because you'll have a truce. You'll probably want to build supply depots near their borders before fighting Guangxi and Yunnan. The only snag will be if Sinkiang decides to join Comintern (in which case, you'll have to fight the Soviet Union to get Sinkiang), but, by 1943 and after annexing all other warlords, you'll easily be able to go toe-to-toe with the Soviet Union - and besides, you'll probably get invited into Allies, which will make it a cakewalk."
  },
  {
   "k": "uzl5nd",
   "en": "Method 3"
  },
